    "notes": "The non-PoE member of the EX2000 series: same 24 x 1G + 4 x SFP+ front end as the EX2028-P, but no PSE controllers, no budget and no poeOut on any port, so a lab that needs to power an access point has to pick the -P model. 44 x 4.4 x 20.9 cm, 2.77 kg, fanless, 19.50 W maximum switch power with traffic. Fully managed Layer 2/3 switch, managed by cloud or on-premises cnMaestro and by an industry-standard CLI, with embedded web management, a DHCP server and client, DHCP relay, OSPFv2 and RIPv1/v2 (static routes and inter-VLAN routing included), LACP/static LAGs, RSTP/MSTP/PVRST, ERPSv1, QinQ, IGMP snooping v1/v2, LLDP/LLDP-MED, 802.1X/MAB, DHCP snooping, dynamic ARP inspection, per-port flow control and storm control. 16 K MAC table, 4 K VLANs, 9 K jumbo frames, 800 MHz CPU, 128 MB flash, 512 MB DRAM, 1.5 MB packet buffer. 100-240 VAC supply, 1U rack mountable, 0-50 C operating, -40 to 70 C storage, 55 C at 95% RH. RS-232 serial console (RJ-45) on every model, plus a USB port and an out-of-band Ethernet management port: the spec table lists the management port but states its rate only for the EX2028-P (10/100 Mbps), so it is recorded here rather than modelled as a data port at a rate no document gives. Sources: cnMatrix EX2000 Series data sheet https://brandcentral.cambiumnetworks.com/asset/c544bc91-c854-4589-a6e6-94864102a2d9/cnMatrix-EX2000-Data-Sheet.pdf and the model page https://www.cambiumnetworks.com/products/switching/cnmatrix-switch-ex2028/."
